From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:21:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: track the previous entry in fetch_cache_get()

last_conn was initialised to NULL and never advanced, so the branch
that unlinks a matched entry from the middle of the list was
unreachable.  A cache hit on any entry but the first therefore ran
"connection_cache = conn->next_cached", dropping every entry ahead of
the match from the list without closing it and leaking its descriptor,
SSL context and buffers.

Advance last_conn as the list is walked.
---
 libfetch/common.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libfetch/common.c b/libfetch/common.c
index 1ab9123..ed7e098 100644
--- a/libfetch/common.c
+++ b/libfetch/common.c
@@ -352,6 +352,7 @@ fetch_cache_get(const struct url *url, int af)
 				connection_cache = conn->next_cached;
 			return conn;
 		}
+		last_conn = conn;
 	}
 
 	return NULL;
